*> Acceptance test US3-1 (spec 002 FR-007, FR-008, FR-009, FR-010; SC-001): the pack screen lists the user's packs,
*> enables, disables and reorders them, and its edge cases show on it: two packs with the same path (the higher
*> one wins, reordering swaps the winner) and a pack removed while enabled (the screen says it is missing).
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. ACC-F2US3-PACK-SCREEN.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-DIR                 PIC X(64) VALUE "build/client-test-f2-pack-screen".
 01 WS-DIR-LENGTH          BINARY-LONG VALUE 32.
 01 WS-NAMES               PIC X(256) VALUE "alpha beta.zip".
 01 WS-ACTION              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ARG                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ANY                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-FOUND               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-GREY                PIC X(80) VALUE "cobolcraft:block/greystone".
 01 WS-GREY-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG VALUE 26.
 01 WS-PIXEL               PIC X(32).
 01 WS-HITS                BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "TEST-PACK-START" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-DIR WS-DIR-LENGTH WS-NAMES
     CALL "TEST-STEP" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE ACT-PACKS TO WS-ACTION
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ANY WS-FOUND
     CALL "TEST-SCREEN-TEXTS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-TEXT
     MOVE "acceptance US3-1 given two packs in resourcepacks/ when the pack screen opens then both are "
         & "listed as available" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE ZERO TO WS-HITS
     INSPECT WS-TEXT TALLYING WS-HITS FOR ALL "Alpha pack" ALL "Beta pack"
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 2 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-HITS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Enable alpha (entry 1), then beta.zip (entry 2): beta on top; Done applies.
     PERFORM ENABLE-ENTRY-1
     PERFORM ENABLE-ENTRY-2
     MOVE ACT-PACKS-DONE TO WS-ACTION
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ANY WS-FOUND
     CALL "TEST-PIXEL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-GREY WS-GREY-LENGTH WS-PIXEL
     MOVE "acceptance US3-1 same path in both packs: the higher pack (beta.zip, enabled last) wins" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "10,10,200,255" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-PIXEL TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Reorder: select beta.zip, Move Down; Done; alpha wins now.
     MOVE ACT-PACKS TO WS-ACTION
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ANY WS-FOUND
     MOVE ACT-SELECT TO WS-ACTION
     MOVE 2 TO WS-ARG
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ARG WS-FOUND
     MOVE ACT-PACK-DOWN TO WS-ACTION
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ANY WS-FOUND
     MOVE ACT-PACKS-DONE TO WS-ACTION
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ANY WS-FOUND
     CALL "TEST-PIXEL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-GREY WS-GREY-LENGTH WS-PIXEL
     MOVE "acceptance US3-1 moving beta.zip down puts alpha on top: its greystone (green) wins" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "10,200,10,255" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-PIXEL TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Disable alpha: beta.zip's greystone shows.
     MOVE ACT-PACKS TO WS-ACTION
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ANY WS-FOUND
     MOVE ACT-SELECT TO WS-ACTION
     MOVE 1 TO WS-ARG
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ARG WS-FOUND
     MOVE ACT-PACK-DISABLE TO WS-ACTION
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ANY WS-FOUND
     MOVE ACT-PACKS-DONE TO WS-ACTION
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ANY WS-FOUND
     CALL "TEST-PIXEL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-GREY WS-GREY-LENGTH WS-PIXEL
     MOVE "acceptance US3-1 disabling alpha leaves beta.zip's greystone (blue)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "10,10,200,255" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-PIXEL TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Remove beta.zip while it is enabled: Done reloads, the screen says it is missing, the built-in look returns.
     CALL "SYSTEM" USING "rm -f build/client-test-f2-pack-screen/resourcepacks/beta.zip"
     MOVE ACT-PACKS TO WS-ACTION
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ANY WS-FOUND
     MOVE ACT-PACKS-DONE TO WS-ACTION
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ANY WS-FOUND
     MOVE ACT-PACKS TO WS-ACTION
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ANY WS-FOUND
     CALL "TEST-STEP" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "TEST-SCREEN-TEXTS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-TEXT
     MOVE ZERO TO WS-HITS
     INSPECT WS-TEXT TALLYING WS-HITS FOR ALL "beta.zip cannot be used: the pack is missing"
     MOVE "acceptance US3-1 a pack zip removed while enabled: the pack screen says it is missing" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-HITS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.

 ENABLE-ENTRY-1.
     MOVE ACT-SELECT TO WS-ACTION
     MOVE 1 TO WS-ARG
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ARG WS-FOUND
     MOVE ACT-PACK-ENABLE TO WS-ACTION
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ANY WS-FOUND.

 ENABLE-ENTRY-2.
     MOVE ACT-SELECT TO WS-ACTION
     MOVE 2 TO WS-ARG
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ARG WS-FOUND
     MOVE ACT-PACK-ENABLE TO WS-ACTION
     CALL "TEST-CLICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ANY WS-FOUND.
 END PROGRAM ACC-F2US3-PACK-SCREEN.
 COPY CLTEST.
 COPY PACKTEST.
